Bottom-Up Approach in Data Warehouse
Important exam topic
1. Definition
The Bottom-Up Approach is a method of designing a Data Warehouse in which we first create smaller Data Marts for individual departments. Later, these Data Marts are integrated to form a centralized Enterprise Data Warehouse (EDW).

In simple words:

First create small department-wise Data Marts, then combine them into one big Data Warehouse.
